Z||000011||Blade||09-07-2000||01:54 PM||||i was gonna post about my idle today and boom i see your post. Here are the symptoms im getting are they similiar to yours? And if anyone has ideas lemme know. Wheni got car it idled real nice at 1000 rpm when warm. now sometimes it shoot up and idles at 2000 rpm or sometimes 1500 and even 2500 a few times. and then it will sometimes go back to 1000. Check engine light comes on for a while then goes off. I plan on chekcing the codes this weekend when i have time to do it right.(never done it) I may do it during lunch today. Any help is apreciated. I think it is running hot because of this. I ordered the 180 thermastat and fanswitch to intall soon as well.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000012||Heisenhund||09-07-2000||02:00 PM||||You describe my symptoms exactly. Only now the only time mine will go back to 1K is when I'm stopped at a light with the A/C on. When you pull the codes I bet you'll find a 35. That's the Idle Air Control valve code, but what sets it is the fact that you're idling more than 50 RPM higher than the ECM says you should. My advice is to check all over for vacuum leaks before you plunk down the $$ for a new IAC. I replaced mine (and just about every other sensor on the car) and the problem still exists.<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000013||Blade||09-07-2000||03:29 PM||||Mine goes down to 1000 intermitently. sometimes 2000 sometimes 1000. AC or no AC. I wondered cuz yours sounds the same probably is the same problem. Another thing is wierd. My temp gauge seems to be off by 20 degrees. I seem to remember it going up to 230-240 or so then kicking down again when it is cooled by fan now it does the same around 210-220. I think it jumped a peg. It is way over to the left when engine is cool now. I gonna check vacume i guese. we see mabe this weekend.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000014||ROB MAC||09-07-2000||03:40 PM||||When checking or cleaning IAC valve , look for hairline cracks in the threads near the base. And to the previous question, the relay is on the inside fender wall beside driver headlight and when it shorts it causes all kinds of electrical problems.||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierocrazy||09-07-2000||10:30 PM||||How do you know its shorted , do you lights go out or anything, my driver side light is real slow when it works?<P>85GT 3.2||||reg||1
Z||000016||Blade||09-08-2000||11:52 AM||||Heisenhund.....this may sound stupid but i checked my oil and it was low added a quart(changing it this weekend i just bought car and was waiting to get some money.) and my idle has improved. I have drove it twice since yesterday and the idle(when warm) has been 1000 and 1500. Check engine light still coming on and i think there is another prob but just thought id mention this since it helped me a lil.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000017||JetroGT||09-09-2000||08:54 AM||||Cracked EGR tube. It's the metal tube running from underneith the left side of the plenum. Sometimes the heat wraping hides the crack.||||reg||3
